# Build context for web/Dockerfile (deploy/docker-compose.yml: context ../web).
#
# Everything listed here is excluded from the tarball Docker sends to the daemon.
# Two reasons it matters: node_modules alone is hundreds of megabytes of context
# that would be reinstalled by `npm ci` anyway, and a stray .env would be copied
# into an image layer where `docker history` can read it back out.

# ─── Dependencies — reinstalled from the lockfile inside the image ─────────
node_modules
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/cache
.yarn/unplugged

# ─── Build output — rebuilt inside the image; a stale .next also poisons it ─
.next
out
build
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ─── Secrets — MUST NOT reach any image layer ──────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ─── VCS / CI / editors ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# ─── Vercel / Turbo local state ────────────────────────────────────────────
.vercel
.turbo

# ─── Tests and coverage — not part of a production build ───────────────────
coverage
.nyc_output
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx

# ─── Docs and OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
README.md
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Never copy the Dockerfile into itself ─────────────────────────────────
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
